		<main>
			<header>
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<h1>I notice things.</h1>
			</header>

			<section class="prose">
				<p>
					Something I Noticed is where I write about things I encounter
					in ordinary life and follow them wherever they lead.
				</p>

				<p>
					Sometimes that starts with cats. Sometimes technology,
					music, cooking, a conversation, or something I was tinkering
					with. I usually don't know where an observation will end
					when I begin writing about it.
				</p>

				<p>
					The point isn't to hand you a philosophy or tell you what
					to think. I'm documenting what I noticed, what I thought
					about it, what I tried, and what changed in my understanding.
				</p>

				<h2>How I make this</h2>

				<p>
					I use contemporary tools as part of my creative process,
					including language models for things such as editing,
					research assistance, coding, and working through ideas.
					When generative tools materially contribute to a piece or
					its visuals, I aim to be transparent about that process.
				</p>

				<p>
					The observations, experiences, judgments, and final
					editorial decisions remain my own.
				</p>
			</section>
		</main>

		<footer>
			<a href="/">Back home</a>
		</footer>
	</body>
